# Aura for Kodi Omega (21.x)

**Aura 2.1.1 source — ALPHA, usable work in progress, unofficial continuation.**

Current source includes the 2.1.1 cast-artwork fix described below. The latest published package is **2.1.0 ALPHA**; the installation links and release hash below still refer to that package, not an unpublished 2.1.1 archive.

This project brings [jurialmunkey's original Aura skin](https://github.com/jurialmunkey/skin.aura) to **Kodi 21 Omega**. The aim is to preserve Aura's familiar appearance and workflow while adapting outdated integrations and Kodi interfaces to current Omega add-ons and APIs.

The skin is in regular use and is generally usable, but **it is not finished**. Some layouts need further work, existing configurations may need attention, and formal end-to-end testing is incomplete. Kodi 21.3 is the development target; compatibility with Kodi 19, 20 or 22 is not claimed for this Omega release.

- **Skin source and issues:** [kcook98765/skin.aura](https://github.com/kcook98765/skin.aura)
- **Recommended installation:** [kcook-lab-repo](https://github.com/kcook98765/kcook-lab-repo)
- **Direct ZIP:** [Aura 2.1.0 ALPHA](https://github.com/kcook98765/kcook-lab-repo/releases/tag/aura-omega-2.1.0-alpha)

## Install Aura

### Option 1 — Install from kcook-lab-repo (recommended)

The repository currently publishes Aura 2.1.0 for its **Omega** catalog. If you already have the `kcook-lab-repo` repository installed, skip to step 4.

1. In Kodi, open **Settings → File manager → Add source**.
2. Enter `https://kcook98765.github.io/kcook-lab-repo/` and name the source `kcook-lab-repo`.
3. Go to **Settings → Add-ons → Install from zip file**, choose the new `kcook-lab-repo` source and install **`repository.ai.kodi-0.1.1.zip`**. If Kodi asks, enable **Unknown sources** under **Settings → System → Add-ons** and acknowledge the warning.
4. Open **Install from repository → kcook-lab-repo → Look and feel → Skin → Aura** and select **Install**.
5. Allow Kodi to resolve the declared dependencies from the official Kodi add-on repository. Once installed, switch to Aura through **Settings → Interface → Skin** if Kodi has not already prompted you.

The repository's display name is **kcook-lab-repo**, but its installer/add-on ID remains `repository.ai.kodi`. You do **not** need a newer installer to see this Aura release. The repository is the preferred option for receiving subsequent published updates through Kodi.

### Option 2 — Download the skin ZIP directly

1. Download **[skin.aura-2.1.0.zip](https://github.com/kcook98765/kcook-lab-repo/releases/download/aura-omega-2.1.0-alpha/skin.aura-2.1.0.zip)** from the [2.1.0 ALPHA release](https://github.com/kcook98765/kcook-lab-repo/releases/tag/aura-omega-2.1.0-alpha).
2. Make the downloaded ZIP accessible to Kodi, then select **Settings → Add-ons → Install from zip file** and choose it. Enable **Unknown sources** if prompted.
3. Allow Kodi to resolve dependencies from the official Kodi add-on repository; if an installation reports missing dependencies, check the list below rather than installing obsolete legacy helper ZIPs.
4. Select Aura from **Settings → Interface → Skin**.

A direct ZIP install is a manual installation method; use the repository method for normal update management. The download is a packaged skin, **not** GitHub's automatically generated *Source code (zip)* archive.

**Release package SHA-256:** `7309fc3f60429e4ba638d36046565ae48fa2b75f56f653df5200a960aa3ce9c0`

## What is retained and what changed

| Area | Omega continuation |
| --- | --- |
| Appearance | The original Aura look, artwork, typography, horizontal home menu, rounded styling and general navigation approach are retained. |
| Home and widgets | Customisable home menus, multiple widgets and Skin Shortcuts-based editing remain central features. Older widgets using removed providers may require manual source reselection. |
| Library and information | Movie, TV and music views remain; current Kodi information/dialog conventions and supported add-ons replace several outdated integrations. |
| Search and metadata | Global Search, Embuary information/helper, TMDb Helper and Skin Info Service provide supported integration paths. Optional online metadata enrichment is **off by default**, so third-party ratings, artwork and awards may not always appear. |
| Settings and controls | Kodi Omega-compatible dialogs, colour selection, favourites, video management and seek-display paths replace older API behavior. The available palette is not identical to legacy automatic artwork-derived colouring. |
| PVR / EPG | PVR/EPG interfaces and event actions have been adapted around current Kodi behavior. Live TV, guide, recordings and backend-specific flows are **not yet comprehensively tested**. |
| Upcoming TV | A library-oriented airing calendar takes the place of old Next Aired-related behavior; it is **not** a feature-for-feature copy of the previous guide. |
| Backup | Uses Kodi's **Backup** add-on in place of historical Skin Helper backup integration. Backup must be configured; old Skin Helper archives are not automatically compatible. |

This is primarily a **compatibility restoration**, not a redesign. Additional features may be developed later, but they should not be assumed available in this alpha.

### Episode cast artwork in 2.1.1 source

Fixes a route-dependent Video Info problem: opening **TV list → series → season → episodes → an episode → Video Info** could repeat the season poster across different cast members, while opening the same episode through **Continue Watching** showed actor portraits. Cast cards now use each actor's artwork without changing general media-poster selection elsewhere.

The focused source regression checks pass. Native acceptance of the corrected bad library route was not completed because the owner requested stopping further testing; this is not a claim of comprehensive native validation.

## Add-ons used by Aura on Omega

The authoritative requirement list is in [`addon.xml`](addon.xml). The following dependencies are declared for current source, unchanged from 2.1.0; Kodi normally handles installation and their additional dependencies:

| Add-on / resource | Role |
| --- | --- |
| **Skin Shortcuts** (`script.skinshortcuts`) | Custom home menus and widgets |
| **Global Search** (`script.globalsearch`) | Search interface |
| **Image Resource Select** (`script.image.resource.select`) | Image-resource selection |
| **Embuary Info** (`script.embuary.info`) | Information views and related functions |
| **Embuary Helper** (`script.embuary.helper`) | Skin helper functionality |
| **TheMovieDb Helper** (`plugin.video.themoviedb.helper`) | Supported metadata and discovery integration |
| **Skin Info Service** (`script.skin.info.service`) | Skin information services |
| **Backup** (`script.xbmcbackup`) | Optional user-initiated backup/restore workflow; declared as an install dependency |
| **White Weather Icons** (`resource.images.weathericons.white`) | Weather icons |
| **Transparent Movie Genre Icons** (`resource.images.moviegenreicons.transparent`) | Genre icons |
| **White Studio Icons** (`resource.images.studios.white`) | Studio logos |

Kodi provides the required `xbmc.gui` interface (minimum declared version **5.17.0**). Although Backup is included in the declared dependencies, **running backups is optional and requires configuration**. Other add-on features may use network services when invoked even with optional enrichment turned off.

**For users moving from older Aura:** do not follow the old manual Skin Helper or CherryPy installation instructions. Saved widgets targeting discontinued providers will not automatically migrate; open the Aura menu/widget editor and reselect those sources as needed. Existing settings are not guaranteed to migrate cleanly.

## Optional ratings and online enrichment

Kodi's native/list-item ratings and stored library metadata are the baseline. The **Enable ratings** choices control which available scores are displayed; enabling every provider there does **not** fetch missing ratings. The **Votes** choice separately controls vote-count display.

To use additional online metadata, enable **Skin Settings → Library → Online metadata enrichment (optional)**, which is **off by default**. Open **Enrichment provider settings** for Skin Info Service and configure a legitimate provider key where required—for example, your own valid **OMDb** key for data supplied by OMDb. Aura does not provision keys or guarantee provider access, title coverage or every score.

Rotten Tomatoes **critics (Tomatometer)** and **audience (Popcornmeter)** are separate scores under the shared display choice. One may be available without the other; unavailable IMDb, TMDb, Metacritic or other provider data may also remain absent. Equal numeric scores from different providers are possible and do not by themselves indicate duplicated data.

## Known limitations and feedback

- **WIP / ALPHA:** minor layouts and functionality still require refinement. Populated-library widgets, playback/OSD variants, PVR/EPG, recordings, games and some migration scenarios lack complete formal acceptance.
- **Existing Aura installations:** the ID is still `skin.aura`. This version is **not** a separate side-by-side skin; changing sources may affect the existing Aura install, update behavior and saved settings.
- **Recovery:** keep Kodi's default **Estuary** skin available. Return through **Settings → Interface → Skin → Estuary** if you encounter a problem. Switching skins does not undo changed widgets or other settings.
- **Backups:** configure Backup with a destination, **Add-on Data** and any custom asset folders, and test recovery before relying on it. Installing Backup by itself does not create a backup.
- **Screenshots:** bundled screenshots are inherited from the older skin and are not up-to-date Omega captures. They also do not meet the official Kodi repository's required screenshot dimensions; this is an **unofficial repository release**, not an official Kodi skin repository submission.

Report reproducible problems via [GitHub Issues](https://github.com/kcook98765/skin.aura/issues). Include the Kodi version, platform, what you were doing and the expected/actual result. Please remove private information from logs or screenshots.

For detailed development/testing limitations, see [Compatibility](docs/COMPATIBILITY.md) and [Testing](docs/TESTING.md). Those documents include historical preparation-stage results and may not reflect the later distribution publication.

